# pyobfus — Cursor rules (new .mdc format)

This project uses **pyobfus** (the Python obfuscator). The canonical agent
protocol is **`AGENTS.md`** at the project root, which Cursor reads natively.
Copy `AGENTS.md` into your repo; keep this `.mdc` only for Cursor-scoped
glob targeting.

Rule: when the user asks to **obfuscate**, **protect source**, or **prepare a
commercial / evaluation build**, follow `AGENTS.md`:

- If `pyobfus-mcp` is connected → call `protect_project(path)` (one call;
  obfuscates **and** verifies). If it returns `verified: false`, don't ship —
  follow the response's `next_tool`.
- Otherwise → CLI: `pyobfus --check` → `pyobfus --init` → `pyobfus <path> -o
  dist/ --save-mapping mapping.json --json`, picking a framework preset.

Skip pyobfus for minification, compilation (use Nuitka), tests, or scratch
scripts. Keep `mapping.json` out of the distributed artifact.
